    "verification": "Per R67 (Drew ruling: same (cardNumber -> player) map on every shared number is a PARALLEL, not a named set), each flagged category's row set was compared against its candidate anchor -- normalised players (split '/', trim, lowercase, sort, dedupe) on every cardNumber. 45 of 59 categories matched their anchor on EVERY number with zero disagreement and zero missing numbers and were folded onto the anchor category with the source's own stated parallel name written into the parallel column (Clear Cut / Exclusives / French Variation / High Gloss / Bronze / Gold / Level 1 / Level 2 / Ruby / Emerald Auto / Black / Printing Plate / Exclusive). 4 more (2007-08 Upper Deck Retro Exclusive/Printing Plate -- Young Guns, UD Canvas Printing Plate -- Young Guns/Legends) matched only after normalising the anchor's own plural/singular section-header inconsistency ('Young Guns' vs 'Young Gun', 'Legends' vs 'Legend' -- the SAME subset, the source's own sibling sections just spelled the header differently) and were folded the same way once verified. 0 mismatches were found anywhere -- no category needed to be held or registered as its own key. Row count is unchanged by the fold (3,089 before and after): each fold only rewrites a row's category and parallel columns, it does not add or drop rows.",
